            {
              "id": "glog-60c240f7-53a0-4ab0-8e93-b4be165c80dd",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "```markdown\n### Description\n\nCVE-2014-2403 is a vulnerability found in the Java SE component of Oracle Java SE (subcomponent: Libraries). This vulnerability allows remote attackers to affect confidentiality, integrity, and availability via unknown vectors related to the Libraries component. The issue is present in Java SE versions prior to 7u55 and 8u5.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Upgrade Java SE**: The primary mitigation strategy is to upgrade to a version of Java SE that is not affected by this vulnerability. Specifically, upgrade to Java SE 7 Update 55 or Java SE 8 Update 5 or later.\n\n2. **Apply Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches provided by Oracle to ensure that your Java environment is protected against known vulnerabilities.\n\n3. **Limit Network Exposure**: Restrict network exposure for all control system devices and/or systems, and ensure that they are not accessible from the internet.\n\n4. **Use Firewalls**: Implement network segmentation and use firewalls to block access to vulnerable systems from untrusted networks.\n\n5. **Monitor and Audit**: Regularly monitor and audit systems for unusual activity that could indicate an attempted or successful exploitation of the vulnerability.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nSince this vulnerability is related to the Java SE Libraries, the fix involves updating the Java runtime environment rather than modifying application source code. Ensure that your application is compatible with the updated Java version and thoroughly test your application after upgrading.\n\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)\n\nPlease ensure that you regularly check for updates and patches for your software components and follow best practices for secure coding and system configuration.\n```"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2014-2403/suse:java:"
                ]
              }
