              "id": "glog-f700be4c-4665-4290-844a-0a2758d632ea",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2021-29569** affects the `tensorflow` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, available on PyPI. This vulnerability arises from an issue in the `tf.raw_ops.SparseFillEmptyRows` operation, where the implementation does not properly validate the input arguments. This can lead to a heap buffer overflow, potentially allowing an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) by crashing the application.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability is patched. The TensorFlow team has addressed this issue in later releases, so upgrading to the latest stable version is advised.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement additional input validation checks in your application to ensure that inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds and types.\n\n3. **Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches and updates to your dependencies to protect against known vulnerabilities.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe TensorFlow team has fixed this issue in later versions by adding proper validation checks for the input arguments in the `SparseFillEmptyRows` operation. If you are unable to upgrade, consider backporting the fix from the TensorFlow repository to your version. The fix involves adding checks to ensure that the input tensors are not malformed and that their dimensions are as expected.\n\n### Relevant Links\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-787](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\nThese resources provide additional information on secure coding practices and common software weaknesses that can help prevent similar vulnerabilities in the future."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2021-29569/pkg:pypi/tensorflow@2.1.0"
                ]
              }
