                "markdown": "```markdown\n### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2021-29553** affects the `tensorflow-gpu` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, which is a part of the TensorFlow library used for machine learning tasks. This vulnerability arises from an issue in the implementation of certain operations that can lead to a denial of service (DoS) or potentially allow for arbitrary code execution. The root cause is improper validation of input data, which can result in buffer overflows or other memory corruption issues.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: The most effective mitigation is to upgrade to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability is patched. Check the TensorFlow GitHub repository or PyPI for the latest secure version.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that all inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds and types.\n\n3. **Use Virtual Environments**: Run TensorFlow within a virtual environment to limit the impact of any potential exploit.\n\n4. **Regular Security Audits**: Conduct regular security audits and code reviews to identify and mitigate vulnerabilities early.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo address this vulnerability, ensure that all input data is validated before being processed by TensorFlow operations. This can involve:\n\n- Adding checks to confirm that input dimensions and types are as expected.\n- Using TensorFlow's built-in functions to sanitize inputs.\n- Applying patches provided by the TensorFlow maintainers that address this specific issue.\n\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\nThis vulnerability is related to the following CWE:\n\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)\n\nPlease ensure to verify the links and their accessibility as they are subject to change.\n```"
