                "text": "",
                "markdown": "```markdown\n### Description\n\nCVE-2013-5849 is a vulnerability in the Java package management tool `pkg` that affects Oracle Solaris. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to affect confidentiality, integrity, and availability via unknown vectors related to the `pkg` component. The specific details of the vulnerability are not publicly disclosed, but it is categorized as a high-severity issue due to its potential impact.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Update and Patch**: Ensure that your system is running the latest version of the software. Oracle has released patches to address this vulnerability, so applying the latest updates is crucial.\n\n2. **Access Control**: Limit access to the `pkg` tool to trusted users only. Implement strict access controls and ensure that only authorized personnel can execute package management commands.\n\n3. **Network Security**: Use firewalls and intrusion detection systems to monitor and restrict unauthorized access to systems running the vulnerable `pkg` component.\n\n4. **Regular Audits**: Conduct regular security audits and vulnerability assessments to identify and mitigate potential security issues.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nSince the vulnerability details are not fully disclosed, a specific source code fix cannot be provided. However, general best practices for secure coding in package management tools include:\n\n- **Input Validation**: Ensure all inputs are validated and sanitized to prevent injection attacks.\n- **Error Handling**: Implement robust error handling to prevent information leakage.\n- **Least Privilege**: Run processes with the least privilege necessary to reduce the impact of a potential compromise.\n\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-284: Improper Access Control](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/284.html)\n\n```"
